Vulnerability Title

Unauthenticated Direct Access to Post Trade Compliance Reports

Risk Level

High

CVSS v3.1 Score (Intranet Application)

7.5 – High

Vector String:
CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N

Vulnerability Category

Broken Access Control / Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR)

OWASP Category

OWASP Top 10 2021 – A01: Broken Access Control
https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control/

Vulnerability Description

The application contains a Post Trade Compliance module that allows authorized users to download compliance reports based on the selected year. During testing, it was observed that when a user downloads a report, the application generates a direct download link for the file.

By copying the generated download URL and pasting it into another browser session where the user is not authenticated, the report file can still be downloaded successfully without requiring login credentials.

This indicates that the application does not enforce proper authentication and authorization checks on the report download endpoint, allowing unauthorized users with the direct link to access sensitive compliance reports.

Impact

Unauthorized users can download sensitive compliance reports without authentication.

Potential exposure of confidential financial and regulatory data.

Could lead to data leakage within or outside the organization.

Attackers may share or distribute sensitive reports without proper authorization.

Compromises the confidentiality of internal compliance information.

Proof of Concept (PoC) Steps

Step 1: Login to the application with a valid user account that has access to the Post Trade Compliance module.

Step 2: Navigate to the Post Trade Compliance section.

Step 3: Select a specific year and download a compliance report.

Step 4: Capture or copy the direct download URL of the report file.

Step 5: Open a new browser session or private/incognito window where no user is authenticated.

Step 6: Paste the copied download link into the browser address bar.

Step 7: Observe that the report file downloads successfully without requiring authentication.

Recommendations

Enforce authentication checks on all file download endpoints.

Validate user session and authorization before allowing file access.

Avoid exposing direct file paths; instead generate secure, time-limited download tokens.

Implement access control validation at the server level for every request.

Use secure file access mechanisms that restrict access only to authorized users.

